      "content": "A. Rice (Oryza sativa)"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "CHAPTER 2: AGRONOMY — CROP PRODUCTION SCIENCE",
      "id": "avw983j"
    },
    {
      "id": "nzuo5c0",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Aspect</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Details</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Botanical Name</p>",
            "<p>Oryza sativa; Family: Poaceae (Gramineae)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Origin</p>",
            "<p>South/Southeast Asia; India is second largest producer (China first)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Season</p>",
            "<p>Kharif (main); Rabi in coastal areas; Boro (winter-spring in NE)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Climate</p>",
            "<p>Tropical/subtropical; mean temp 22–32°C; 150–200 cm annual rainfall</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Soil</p>",
            "<p>Heavy clayey soil; waterlogged paddies; pH 5.5–6.5</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Seed Rate</p>",
            "<p>80–100 kg/ha (transplanting); 100–120 kg/ha (direct seeding)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Spacing</p>",
            "<p>20 cm × 15 cm; or 20 cm × 20 cm</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Fertiliser (N:P:K)</p>",
            "<p>120:60:60 kg/ha (irrigated); 80:40:40 kg/ha (rainfed)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Water Requirement</p>",
            "<p>1200–2000 mm total; 5 cm standing water maintained in paddy</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Major Varieties</p>",
            "<p>IR-36, IR-64, Pusa Basmati-1, Swarna (MTU-7029), Jaya, Sona Masoori</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>HYV Varieties</p>",
            "<p>IR-8 (first Green Revolution variety), Jyoti, Ratna, Padma</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Major States</p>",
            "<p>WB, UP, Andhra Pradesh, Punjab, Bihar, Odisha, Chhattisgarh</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Major Diseases</p>",
            "<p>Blast (Pyricularia oryzae), BLB (Xanthomonas), Brown Spot (Helminthosporium)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Major Pests</p>",
            "<p>Stem borer (Scirpophaga), Brown Planthopper (BPH), Gall Midge</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Weed Management</p>",
            "<p>Butachlor, Pretilachlor (pre-emergence); 2,4-D (post-emergence)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uildgup",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "B. Wheat (Triticum aestivum)"
    },
    {
      "id": "usr30yd",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Aspect</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Details</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Botanical Name</p>",
            "<p>Triticum aestivum (common bread wheat); T. durum (pasta wheat); Family: Poaceae</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Season</p>",
            "<p>Rabi crop; sown October–November; harvested March–April</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Climate</p>",
            "<p>Cool and moist growing season; warm and dry at ripening; 10–15°C at sowing</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Soil</p>",
            "<p>Well-drained loamy to clayey loam; pH 6.0–7.5; cannot tolerate waterlogging</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Seed Rate</p>",
            "<p>100–125 kg/ha (timely sown); 125–150 kg/ha (late sown)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Fertiliser (N:P:K)</p>",
            "<p>120:60:40 kg/ha (normal); 150:75:50 kg/ha (late sown irrigated)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Irrigation</p>",
            "<p>Crown root initiation (21 days), tillering, jointing, flowering, milk/dough stages</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Major HYV</p>",
            "<p>Kalyan Sona, Sonalika (first HYVs); HD-2781, HD-2967, GW-322, PBW-343, WH-147</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dwarf Varieties</p>",
            "<p>IARI developed; short stem; high-yielding; respond well to fertilisers</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Major States</p>",
            "<p>UP, Punjab, Haryana, MP, Bihar, Rajasthan</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Diseases</p>",
            "<p>Rust (Yellow/Brown/Black — Puccinia spp.), Loose Smut, Karnal Bunt, Powdery Mildew</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Harvest Index</p>",
            "<p>0.4–0.55 in modern HYV; measures economic yield to biological yield ratio</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
